"hadiths[60]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2736,"Narrated 'Ali:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There are six courtesies due from a Muslim to another Muslim: To give Salam to him when he meets him"
2737,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There are six things due from the believer to another believer: Visiting him when he is ill"
2738,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Qutaybah narrated to us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from his brother — and he is Hammām ibn Munabbih — who said:**

""I heard Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) say: 'There is no one among the Companions of the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) who narrated more hadith from the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) than I, except ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr (may Allāh be pleased with him), for he used to write [the hadith down], whereas I did not write.'""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""This is a *hasan sahīh* hadith. And Wahb ibn Munabbih narrated from his brother, who is Hammām ibn Munabbih.""

---

**Note:** This narration highlights the remarkable memory of Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him), who preserved and transmitted an extraordinary number of ahadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) despite not committing them to writing, unlike ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr (may Allāh be pleased with him), who supplemented his memory with written documentation."
2739,"Narrated Abu Musa:The Jews used to sneeze in the presence of the Prophet (ﷺ) hoping that he would say: 'Yarhamukumullah (May Allah have mercy upon you).' So he said: 'Yahdikumullahu Wa Yuslihu Balakum (May Allah guide you and rectify your affairs)"
2740,"Narrated Salim bin 'Ubaid:that he was with some people on a journey"
2741,"Narrated Abu Ayyub:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When one of you sneezes let him say: 'Al-Hamdulillahi 'Ala Kulli Hal (All praise is due to Allah in every circumstance).' And let the one replying to him say: ""Yarhamukallah (May Allah have mercy upon you).' And let him say to him: 'Yahdikumullah Wa Yuslihu Balakum (May Allah guide you and rectify your affairs)"
2742,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet (ﷺ); he responded to one of them and did not respond to the other. The one who was not responded to said: ""O Messenger of Allah! You responded to this person and did not respond to me?' So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""He praised Allah while you did not praise Him"
2743,"Narrated Iyas bin Salamah:from his father: ""A man sneezed in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while I was present"
2744,"Narrated by Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

""Whoever calls to guidance shall have a reward equal to the rewards of those who follow him, without that diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever calls to misguidance shall bear a sin equal to the sins of those who follow him, without that diminishing anything from their sins.""

Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith."
2745,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that when the Prophet (ﷺ) would sneeze, he would cover his face with his hand or with his garment, and muffle the sound with it."
2746,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The sneeze is from Allah and the yawn is from Ash-Shaitan. So when one of you yawns let him cover his mouth with his hand. For when he says 'Ah"
2747,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah loves sneezing and He dislikes the yawn. So when one of you sneezes and says 'Al-Hamdulillah (All praise is due to Allah)"
2748,"Muslim bin Hatim Al-Ansari Al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari narrated to us, from his father, from Ali bin Zaid, from Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Anas bin Malik said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: 'O my son, if you are able to spend your morning and evening with no deceit in your heart towards anyone, then do so.' Then he said to me: 'O my son, that is part of my Sunnah, and whoever revives my Sunnah has loved me, and whoever loves me will be with me in Paradise.'"" And there is a lengthy story connected with this Hadith.

Abu Eisa said: This Hadith is Hasan Ghareeb from this route. Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari is trustworthy, his father is trustworthy, and Ali bin Zaid is truthful, except that he sometimes reports as connected (marfu') something that others report as stopped (mawquf) [at the level of the companion].

He said: And I heard Muhammad bin Bashshar saying: Abu Al-Walid said: Shu'bah said: ""Ali bin Zaid narrated to us, and he used to raise reports (i.e., report them as marfu')."" And we do not know of any narration from Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab from Anas except this lengthy Hadith. Abbad bin Maisarah Al-Minqari has also narrated this Hadith from Ali bin Zaid from Anas, without mentioning Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab in it.

Abu Eisa said: I discussed it with Muhammad bin Ismail, and he did not know of it, and this Hadith - nor any other - is known to have been narrated by Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab from Anas. Anas bin Malik died in the year ninety-three, and Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab died two years after him, in the year ninety-five."
2749,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Let one of you not have his brother stand from his seat then sit in it"
2750,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Let one of you not have his brother stand from his seat then sit in it"
2751,"Narrated Wahb bin Hudaifah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""A man has more right to his seat. If he leaves for some need of his"
2752,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""It is not lawful for a man to separate two people except with their permission"
2753,"Narrated Abu Miljaz:that a man sat in the middle of a circle so Hudhaifah said: ""Cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad - or - Cursed"
2754,"Narrated Anas:""There was no person more beloved to them than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)."" [He said:] ""And they would not stand when they saw him because they knew that he disliked that"
2755,"Narrated Abu Miljaz:that Mu'awiyah came out and 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair and Ibn Safwan stood for him when they saw him"
2756,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Five are from the Fitrah: Cutting the pubic hair"
2757,"Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Ten are from the Fitrah: Paring the mustache"
2758,"Narrated by Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you shall not enter Paradise until you believe, and you shall not truly believe until you love for one another. Shall I not guide you to a deed which, if you practice it, you will love one another? Spread peace (as-salam) among yourselves.""

This hadith is also narrated through other chains from Abdullah ibn Salam, Shurayh ibn Hani from his father, Abdullah ibn Amr, al-Bara, Anas, and Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them all).

Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith."
2759,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""[The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)] fixed the time for us paring the mustache"
2760,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Abū Sa'īd (may Allāh be pleased with him):**

Abū Mūsā (may Allāh be pleased with him) sought permission to enter upon ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him). He said, ""As-salāmu ʿalaykum — may I enter?"" ʿUmar replied, ""That is one."" Then he remained silent for a while, and again said, ""As-salāmu ʿalaykum — may I enter?"" ʿUmar replied, ""That is two."" Then he remained silent for a while and said, ""As-salāmu ʿalaykum — may I enter?"" ʿUmar replied, ""That is three."" Then Abū Mūsā turned back. ʿUmar said to the gatekeeper, ""What did he do?"" He replied, ""He went back."" ʿUmar said, ""Bring him to me."" When he came, ʿUmar asked, ""What is this that you have done?"" He replied, ""The Sunnah."" ʿUmar said, ""The Sunnah? By Allāh, you must bring me proof or evidence for this, or I shall surely punish you.""

Abū Sa'īd (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: ""He came to us while we were a group of the Ansār and said, 'O assembly of the Ansār, are you not the most knowledgeable of people regarding the hadīth of the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him)? Did not the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) say: **""Seeking permission (al-isti'dhān) is to be done three times. If permission is granted to you, then enter; otherwise, return""**?'"" The people began to jest with him. Abū Sa'īd (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: ""Then I raised my head toward him and said, 'Whatever punishment has befallen you in this matter, I am your partner in it.'"" He said: ""So he went to ʿUmar and informed him of that, and ʿUmar said, 'I was not aware of this.'""

**In this chapter, there are also narrations from ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him) and Umm Tāriq, the freedwoman of Sa'd.**

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī, may Allāh have mercy on him) said: ""This is a hasan sahīh hadīth. Al-Jurayrī's name is Sa'īd ibn Iyās, and his kunya is Abū Mas'ūd. Others have also narrated this from Abū Nadrah. Abū Nadrah al-ʿAbdī's name is al-Mundhir ibn Māliq ibn Qut'ah."""
2761,"Narrated Zaid bin Arqam:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever does not take from his mustache"
2762,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him):**

A man entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was sitting in a corner of the mosque. The man performed prayer, then came and offered salutations upon him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **""And upon you. Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.""**

He then narrated the hadith in its entirety.

**Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said:** This is a *hasan* (good) hadith.

Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated this from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar from Sa'id al-Maqburi, and he said: **""from his father, from Abu Hurayrah,""** and he did not mention in it **""then he offered salutations upon him,""** and he said: **""And upon you.""**

He (Abu Isa) said: **The hadith of Yahya ibn Sa'id is more authentic (aṣaḥḥ).**

---

*Note: This is the well-known hadith of the man who performed his prayer improperly, which the Prophet ﷺ instructed to repeat his prayer multiple times, and in which the Prophet ﷺ subsequently taught him the correct manner of performing the prayer.*"
2763,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Trim the mustache and leave the beard to grow"
2764,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered trimming the mustache and leaving the beard to grow"
2765,"Qutaybah narrated to us, Ibn Luḥayʿah narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:

""He is not one of us who imitates other than us. Do not imitate the Jews or the Christians, for the greeting of the Jews is a gesture with the fingers, and the greeting of the Christians is a gesture with the palms.""

Abū ʿĪsā said: This hadith has a weak chain of narration. And Ibn al-Mubārak narrated this hadith from Ibn Luḥayʿah but did not raise it (i.e., did not attribute it to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him)."
2766,"Narrated Jabir:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited Ishtimal As-Samma"
2767,"Narrated Jabir:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited Ishtimal As-Samma"
2768,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw a man laying on his stomach so he said: ""Indeed such laying is not loved by Allah"
2769,"Narrated Bahz bin Hakim:""My father narrated to me from my grandfather"
2770,"Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:""I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) reclining upon as pillow"
2771,"Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:""I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) reclining upon a pillow"
2772,"Narrated Abu Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""A man is not lead in his dominion"
2773,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Buraidah:""I heard my father Buraidah saying: 'I was walking with the Prophet (ﷺ) when a man came to him with a donkey"
2774,"Narrated Jabir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Do you have Anmat?"" I said: ""Where would we get Anmat from?"" He said: ""Soon you will have Anmat"" He said: ""I would say to my wife: 'Remove your Anmat from my sight.' But she would say: 'Did not the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: ""Indeed you shall soon have Anmat?"" He said: ""So I left it"
2775,"Narrated Iyas bin Salamah:from his father who said: ""I guided Allah's Prophet (ﷺ) and Al-Hasan and Al-Husain"
2776,"Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:""I asked the Messenger Of Allah (ﷺ) about the unintentional glance"
2777,"Narrated Ibn Buraidah:from his father (from the Prophet (ﷺ)) who said: ""O 'Ali! Do not follow a look with a look"
2778,"Narrated Nabhan the freed slave of Umm Salamah:to Ibn Shihab, that Umm Salamah narrated to him, that she and Maimunah were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), she said: ""So when we were with him, Ibn Umm Maktum came, and he entered upon him, and that was after veiling had been ordered for us. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Veil yourselves from him.' So I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Is he not blind such that he can not see us or recognize us?' So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Are you two blind such that you can not see him?'"""
2779,"Narrated Dhakwan:from the freed slave of 'Amr bin Al-'As that 'Amr bin Al-'As sent him to 'Ali seeking his permission to enter upon Asma bint Umais"
2780,"Narrated Sufyān ibn Wakīʿ, narrated Rawḥ ibn ʿUbādah, from Ibn Jurayj, ʿAmr ibn Abī Sufyān informed me that ʿAmr ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣafwān informed him that Kaladah ibn Ḥanbal informed him that Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah sent him with milk, young camel meat, and *ḍaghābīs* to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, while the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, was at the upper part of the valley. He said: ""I entered upon him without greeting him with salām and without seeking permission. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: 'Go back and say: *As-salāmu ʿalaykum, may I enter?*' This was after Ṣafwān had embraced Islam."" ʿAmr said: ""Umayyah ibn Ṣafwān also narrated this hadith to me, but he did not say, 'I heard it from Kaladah.'"" Abū ʿĪsā said: ""This is a *ḥasan gharīb* hadith; we do not know it except from the hadith of Ibn Jurayj. Abū ʿĀṣim also narrated it from Ibn Jurayj in the same manner. *Ḍaghābīs* is a type of edible herb."""
2781,"Narrated Humaid bin 'Abdur-Rahman:that he heard Mu'awiyah giving a Khutbah in Al-Madinah"
2782,"Narrated 'Abdullah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) cursed the women who practice tattooing and those who seek to be tattooed"
2783,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Allah's curse is upon the woman who lengthens hair and the women who seeks to have her hair lengthened"
2784,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the women who imitate men and the men who imitate women"
2785,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed those men who behave effeminately and those women whose behavior is masculine"
2786,"Narrated Abu Musa:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Every eye commits adultery"
2787,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Fragrance for men is that which its scent is apparent and its color is hidden"
2788,"Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:""The Prophet (ﷺ) said [to me]: 'Indeed the best fragrance for men is what's scent is apparent and its color is hidden"
2789,"Narrated Thumamah bin 'Abdullah:""Anas would not refuse perfume"
2790,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There are three that are not refused: Cushions"
2791,"Narrated Abu 'Uthman An-Nahdi:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'When one of you is given some fragrance then do not refuse it"
2792,"Narrated 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""A woman is not to touch a woman such that she can describe her to her husband as if he is looking at her"
2793,"Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Sa'eed [Al-Khudri] from his father who said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'A man is not to look at the 'Awrah of a man"
2794,"# Hadith of the Three Men Who Entered the Mosque

**Narrated by Abu Waqid al-Laithy (may Allah be pleased with him):**

The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was once sitting in the mosque with the people around him when three men approached. Two of them came forward to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and gave him salām, while the third departed and left.

As for the first of the two, he noticed a gap in the circle and sat within it. As for the second, he sat behind them. As for the third, he turned away and left.

When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had finished, he said:

**""Shall I not inform you about the three men? As for one of them, he sought refuge in Allah, so Allah granted him refuge. As for the other, he felt shy (modest), so Allah showed modesty (mercy) toward him. As for the other, he turned away, so Allah turned away from him.""**

---

**Abu Eisa (al-Tirmidhi, may Allah have mercy on him) said:** This is a *hasan sahih* (good and authentic) hadith.

**Note on the narrators:**

- **Abu Waqid al-Laithy** (may Allah be pleased with him) — his name is al-Harith ibn Awf.
- **Abu Murrah**, the freed slave (mawlā) of Umm Hani bint Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with her) — his name is Yazid. He is also referred to as the freed slave of Aqil ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him).

---

*Related in Jāmi' al-Tirmidhi.*"
2795,"Narrated Zur'ah bin Muslim bin Jardah Al-Aslami:about his grandfather Jarhad"
